WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Translator: Viktor Morandini
Reviewer: Reka Vegi

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:11.271
[Viktor Morandini:
Ready-to-assemble happiness]

00:00:15.721 --> 00:00:19.382
Believe it or not, 
I've found the secret to happiness

00:00:20.402 --> 00:00:23.481
all I needed was
ten shrinks to treat me.

00:00:25.301 --> 00:00:30.199
Okay, they didn't treat me;
we just went to Swedish class together.

00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:33.641
But I really needed one of them

00:00:33.641 --> 00:00:36.290
to ask me this question
at some point during the course:

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:39.742
"Viktor, you always seem
so calm and happy.

00:00:39.742 --> 00:00:41.111
What is your secret?"

00:00:42.411 --> 00:00:45.552
And if a shrink ask you this, 
you have to take it seriously.

00:00:45.552 --> 00:00:47.471
So, I really looked into myself.

00:00:48.551 --> 00:00:54.542
And realized that
it's all my mother's fault.

00:00:54.542 --> 00:00:56.362
(Laughter)

00:00:57.082 --> 00:00:59.434
Even though my mom
is more or less pure Hungarian,

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:02.244
she works as a Swedish teacher,
interpreter, and translator.

00:01:02.244 --> 00:01:04.175
Therefore she raised us the "IKEA" way.

00:01:04.175 --> 00:01:05.686
(Laughter)

00:01:06.426 --> 00:01:09.926
Besides a love of stylish furniture
and meatballs,

00:01:10.886 --> 00:01:13.957
she also sowed the seeds
of positive attitude into our lives.

00:01:14.187 --> 00:01:17.516
I would like to share it's essence today

00:01:18.506 --> 00:01:21.047
Actually, I can sum it up in one sentence:

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.776
[“Det finns inget dåligt väder,
bara dåliga kläder.”]

00:01:23.776 --> 00:01:25.075
(Laughter)

00:01:25.129 --> 00:01:26.969
(Applause)

00:01:32.765 --> 00:01:35.163
No, this is not the name of our 
kitchen furniture.

00:01:35.163 --> 00:01:36.514
(Laughter)

00:01:37.194 --> 00:01:41.277
It's a Swedish proverb,
it means:

00:01:41.277 --> 00:01:44.155
"There is no bad weather, 
only wrong clothes."

00:01:45.669 --> 00:01:47.755
It took me about 15 years to realize

00:01:47.755 --> 00:01:50.455
that they don't mean it 
only for the weather exclusively

00:01:50.455 --> 00:01:52.205
but for everything in life.

00:01:52.625 --> 00:01:55.545
That your attitude is decisive,

00:01:55.545 --> 00:01:58.686
and nothing is as bad
as it seems for first.

00:01:58.686 --> 00:02:02.254
I am lucky, I always had a raincoat,
a pair of rain boots,

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:05.125
ever since I was a child.

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:08.627
Therefore on rainy days, 
we didn't have to stay home

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:12.327
we just had to put on the rainwear,
and could go jump in the puddles.

00:02:13.877 --> 00:02:16.210
As a 29-year-old project manager

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:19.570
unfortunately, I cannot hop
from puddle to puddle to the office,

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:23.021
but I still have a raincoat,

00:02:23.021 --> 00:02:25.839
touch screen gloves,
and a water-resistant phone,

00:02:25.839 --> 00:02:28.871
making my morning routine 
weather resistant.

00:02:31.401 --> 00:02:34.695
The idea of "No bad weather,
only wrong clothes,"

00:02:34.695 --> 00:02:38.525
is also great to protect you from
the most dangerous Hungarian question:

00:02:39.305 --> 00:02:42.333
"How are you doing?"

00:02:42.333 --> 00:02:44.563
(Laughter)

00:02:44.563 --> 00:02:49.472
Maybe you have noticed it, 
that too many Hungarians think

00:02:49.472 --> 00:02:53.374
that "How are you?" is a command
to flood you with their complaints.

00:02:53.374 --> 00:02:54.944
(Laughter)

00:02:55.924 --> 00:02:59.892
Contrary to this, up in the North,

00:02:59.892 --> 00:03:03.182
it's impolite to answer this question
with a complaint.

00:03:03.962 --> 00:03:07.102
Therefore I try to find something positive

00:03:07.102 --> 00:03:10.472
every day until I arrive at work.

00:03:10.472 --> 00:03:13.203
Like, "Having tailwind on the bicycle
on the way to work."

00:03:13.203 --> 00:03:14.183
(Laughter)

00:03:15.383 --> 00:03:17.724
or, "A random person
smiled at me on the bus."

00:03:19.594 --> 00:03:21.993
This way I can fend off 
this dangerous question.

00:03:22.093 --> 00:03:25.395
But there is something even more
dangerous to your happiness:

00:03:25.565 --> 00:03:27.153
all those people around us.

00:03:28.303 --> 00:03:32.734
The biggest problem with people
is that everyone is stupid.

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:34.113
(Laughter)

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:39.414
You there, you there,
you in the back, and me too.

00:03:39.414 --> 00:03:44.689
(Applause)

00:03:47.449 --> 00:03:50.745
Let me elaborate on this:
everyone is stupid in their own way.

00:03:51.365 --> 00:03:55.316
I didn't learn this from the Swedes,
I first observed it on them.

00:03:56.906 --> 00:03:59.987
Luckily they also provide a solution, 
coming on "moose back."

00:04:01.547 --> 00:04:05.728
Only one word: "Personkemi."

00:04:06.568 --> 00:04:08.310
The "chemistry of people."

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:13.499
The Swedes, or at least my mom,
don't use it only in romantic relations

00:04:13.499 --> 00:04:14.811
but for all people.

00:04:15.491 --> 00:04:16.992
Because let's be honest

00:04:16.992 --> 00:04:19.503
we often have a negative
first impression of people

00:04:19.503 --> 00:04:22.981
and we can't imagine
how we are going to work with that guy.

00:04:22.981 --> 00:04:26.261
That's when "personkemi," the raincoat 
of the soul comes in handy.

00:04:27.051 --> 00:04:29.213
There are people who seem unlikable

00:04:29.213 --> 00:04:32.174
at first, second, third,
and often tenth sight, too.

00:04:32.174 --> 00:04:35.182
For example my favorite bureaucrat 
at the Stockholm University,

00:04:35.182 --> 00:04:39.070
who just could not ever give
a proper answer to my questions.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:41.892
And when I felt like

00:04:41.892 --> 00:04:44.774
beating the answer out of him with
a bag of frozen meatballs,

00:04:44.774 --> 00:04:46.254
(Laughter)

00:04:47.204 --> 00:04:49.666
that's when my mother's words 
came to my mind.

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:54.055
"My little darling, personkemi!

00:04:55.175 --> 00:04:58.456
You are probably never going to 
start liking this person,

00:04:58.456 --> 00:04:59.655
but you don't have to.

00:05:00.385 --> 00:05:04.164
Just concentrate on the task
and common goal you want to achieve,

00:05:04.164 --> 00:05:05.705
keep this in your mind.

00:05:06.325 --> 00:05:09.875
And don't worry you will meet many 
more people like him in your life.

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:12.296
Believe me, I know, 
I am raising four teenagers."

00:05:12.296 --> 00:05:13.536
(Laughter)

00:05:14.796 --> 00:05:15.987
And it worked!

00:05:15.987 --> 00:05:19.586
With the power of personkemi
I have upped my game,

00:05:19.586 --> 00:05:24.037
and needed to ask everything only about 
five times to get the right answer.

00:05:25.487 --> 00:05:28.556
Besides having a raincoat 
for my body and soul

00:05:28.556 --> 00:05:32.756
I boost my mood with little
crumbs of happiness.

00:05:32.756 --> 00:05:35.476
We have a ritual with my wife for example,

00:05:35.476 --> 00:05:39.197
that we have practiced on almost 
all 76 days of our marriage.

00:05:39.197 --> 00:05:41.127
(Laughter)

00:05:42.197 --> 00:05:47.067
Unlike most married couple,
every night we...

00:05:47.067 --> 00:05:48.866
(Laughter)

00:05:49.216 --> 00:05:53.026
... every night we tell each other 
the good things that happened to us.

00:05:53.026 --> 00:05:54.206
(Laughter)

00:05:55.316 --> 00:05:59.619
Ten days ago, unfortunately,
we had the chance to test this for real,

00:05:59.619 --> 00:06:04.548
because on November 9th,
I had the worst day of my life.

00:06:04.548 --> 00:06:08.059
Three traumatic events happened to me, 
and even the least bad one

00:06:08.059 --> 00:06:10.789
was Donald Trump being elected president.

00:06:10.789 --> 00:06:11.919
(Laughter)

00:06:11.949 --> 00:06:14.780
(Applause)

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:23.559
And when I was giving up on that day
as a 100 per cent awful one,

00:06:23.559 --> 00:06:27.849
Hanga, my wife, reminded me 
to try the evening ritual.

00:06:28.629 --> 00:06:30.960
To my biggest surprise,

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:34.470
we could recollect 11 good things
that happened to us that day.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:37.690
It was still the worst day of our lives,

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:40.550
and I hope we won't outmatch it 
in the near future,

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:45.369
but this helped us to end
the day on a positive note.

00:06:45.369 --> 00:06:49.488
And I put on my blue-yellow raincoat 
with a smile on my face next day.

00:06:51.328 --> 00:06:54.222
After ensuring my own happiness,

00:06:54.222 --> 00:06:57.110
I share it with others
like a good Scandinavian.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:01.770
So, the people around me 
will be happier too,

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:03.969
which is good for all of us.

00:07:03.969 --> 00:07:06.460
And of course happiness is like a diet:

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:09.571
If you post it on Facebook,
tell it to your colleagues

00:07:09.571 --> 00:07:13.977
or give a TEDx speech about it,
then it is much easier to stick to it.

00:07:14.597 --> 00:07:18.121
With this, we have the last piece
of the Ready-To-Assemble Happiness.

00:07:18.701 --> 00:07:22.423
Maybe it only fits into
my living room perfectly

00:07:22.423 --> 00:07:25.952
and not all 600 of you will storm
to the closest IKEA to buy rainwear

00:07:25.952 --> 00:07:27.381
after my speech.

00:07:28.591 --> 00:07:31.341
But I truly hope that next time

00:07:31.341 --> 00:07:35.065
when you wake up to a foggy,
damp, rainy, really crappy Monday...

00:07:35.065 --> 00:07:39.544
(Laughter)

00:07:39.544 --> 00:07:42.257
(Applause)

00:07:46.943 --> 00:07:49.936
So on that next crappy Monday
I hope you will remember,

00:07:49.936 --> 00:07:52.357
what the skinny kid told you
about raincoats.

00:07:52.357 --> 00:07:53.337
(Laughter)

00:07:53.337 --> 00:07:54.668
And weather.

00:07:54.668 --> 00:07:57.509
That there is no bad weather 
only the wrong clothes.

00:07:57.509 --> 00:08:02.598
(Applause)

